 "id": "ancestor-line",
 "text": "I am new here and need help with my family from Croatia. I live outside Croatia, so it is hard. I'm trying to track down my great grandparents and beyond. My great grandfather is Josip PERKOVIĆ and his wife, my great grandmother is Barbara, born LONČAR. That is nearly all I know about them. They're born likely 1900s and Married late 1920s. They had 5 children and one of them is my grandma born 1944. They lived in Dreznik near Nova Gradiska. I think one of their sons, Stjepan, moved away to Austria while my grandma went to Austria too, then Bosnia and finally settling in Macedonia after she married. The 3 kids stayed in Croatia. If anyone recognises them, or has them in a tree, please say, as I cannot get further back. And their 5 kids are Katica, Zora, Anica, Stjepan, and one unknown brother. I have put a picture of Barbara with two of her daughters beside her, Katica and Anica if that helps.",
